Date: Mon, 20 Dec 93 17:19:39 PST
From: Blanc Weber <blancw@microsoft.com>
Subject: PPLs?

My comment/inquiry on PPLs:

" (I would have thought that trans-human types
would be able to enlighten the clueless with superior arguments on a
higher, rarified intellectual level.  But, perhaps trans-psychology is
still too far in the future, although I'm sure everyone is working on it.)"

>From Tim May's reply:

"I hope this helped. Me, I'm not necessarily a fan of PPLs here on this
List (like I said above, it's a poor facsimile of reality),. . . ."

My goodness, what a thorough reply!  I think understand, now, thanks.

"... but something has to be done to replace the current system which favors
flamers who launch ad hominem attacks (amateur psychoanalysis of
"nerds" like me, announcements of Scrooge-like "nauseating" behavior,
trivialization of basic Extropians goals of living longer and
accumulating wealth, etc.) and who, when flamed back, run crying to
Harry crying "He flamed me!" so that people like me, who never file
charges (except the time I did, last September, to make the point that
the system is deeply flawed) are then kicked off the List."
..............................

Further comment on the above paragraph, and the whole subject of 
psychological attacks:

This resembles the problems which exist in living in the real world 
with those whose philosophies and manners are unlike one's own:  how to 
deal with the results of living in freedom with those who will become 
"worse" rather than "better" in their liberty to develop as they will;  
how to defend oneself against those who misunderstand what one says or 
does, who classify it as resulting from evil or malicious motives (the 
problems of free association in a free society).

Unless a system of 'protection' is set up, or unless a group can set up 
residence in a closed society - preferably physically removed from 
other groups/societies  -  then each individual has to come the aid of 
their own dignity.  In a free-wheeling list such as this one, where I 
expected everyone to be free to speak openly, I didn't think it would 
enter anyone's mind to prevent another from doing so.  Is there not a 
trans-human, extropian method of conveying meaning to those who are 
psychologically challenged in comprehending it?  Maybe not yet, but 
this appears to me to be a problem looking for a different kind of 
solution, in terms of the kind of communication used to resolve a 
misunderstanding about meaning.  Something other than the fabrication 
of artificial rules to be enforced.

Going beyond the sense of insult to a clarification of ideas, I think 
would be effective (and not necessarily requiring a whole 'tribunal'  - 
 I don't know how this is done in cyberspace).  Except with truly 
incorrigibles, and who would want to seriously pursue a conversation 
with them, anyway.

Blanc

